# CARRA — MASTER APPLICATION GENERATION PROMPT
## AI-Powered Career Guidance, Discovery and Student Development Platform for Zambia

### 1. YOUR ROLE AND MISSION

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, product architect, UI/UX designer, database engineer, AI integration specialist, accessibility specialist, software tester, and deployment engineer.

Your task is to design and implement CARRA, a complete, extensible, production-oriented web application that helps secondary school students in Zambia discover career paths, understand educational requirements, develop useful skills, and make informed decisions about their futures.

Do not create a landing-page-only demonstration, static prototype, disconnected collection of screens, or dashboard filled with fake statistics.

Build a cohesive application in which the main pages, navigation, search, forms, career catalogue, recommendation engine, saved careers, student dashboard, and learning resources work together.

The application must have a clean codebase that can be exported from Google AI Studio, uploaded to GitHub, installed on another computer, run locally, and deployed independently of Google AI Studio.

Implement the actual application files. Do not stop after providing a project plan, architecture description, wireframe, or sample code.

If a feature requires an external API, database, authentication provider, or secret key that is not configured, implement the appropriate integration boundary, explain what remains to be configured, and provide a working fallback wherever reasonable. Never pretend that an unconfigured service is operational.

